# Falling body under quadratic air drag, released from rest in still air
law terminal_velocity_quadratic_drag
kind research
claim a body of mass m released from rest falls under gravity g against quadratic drag
claim its downward speed approaches v_t = sqrt(2 m g / (rho cd area)) as v_t tanh(g t / v_t)
source ALICE-Physics tests/analytic_wind_zone_terminal_velocity.rs:25 (v_t), :57 (8 time constants), :68 (rel err < 1e-3)

input m kg range 0.1 1000
input g m/s^2 range 1 30
input rho kg/m^3 range 0.1 2
input cd 1 range 0.1 3
input area m^2 range 0.01 10
input t s
x-list t                      # t is a sequence of sample times; the law holds at every element

let v_t m/s = sqrt(2*m*g/(rho*cd*area))
let tau s = v_t/g
let t_over_tau 1 = t/tau
x-range t_over_tau 0 8        # valid range on a derived quantity: 0 <= t / tau <= 8

x-state v m/s                 # simulated state: downward speed
x-initial v = 0
x-ode v m/s^2 = g - rho*cd*area*v^2/(2*m)
x-method free                 # the integration method and internal step are the implementer's choice

output v m/s = v_t*(1 - exp(-2*t/tau))/(1 + exp(-2*t/tau))
tolerance v m/s = 0.001*v_t

oracle v m=10 g=10 rho=1 cd=2 area=1 t=8 -> 9.999997749296758 within 1e-9

verdict conforms when every reported v(t) is within the tolerance of the output expression
verdict an input outside its range, or any t with t / tau outside [0, 8], is rejected
